## 92. Algebraic Conjecture Optimization


### 19.1 Definition

ACO is Paracine's typed, effect-aware algebraic optimization system.

It discovers candidate computational equivalences and establishes their legality before transformation.

ACO integrates:

- Typed E-graphs.
- Equality saturation.
- Abstract interpretation.
- Structural pattern discovery.
- Closure escape analysis.
- Defunctionalization.
- Environment scalarization.
- Partial evaluation.
- Currying collapse.
- Chain fusion.
- Traversal fusion.
- Resource-aware extraction.
- Translation validation.
- Native profitability evaluation.

### 19.2 Conjecture lifecycle

```text
Verified Program Facts
          |
          v
Candidate Equivalence
          |
          v
Typed Context Analysis
          |
          v
Ownership / Effects / Traps
Numerics / Security / ABI
          |
          v
Proof Obligations
          |
          v
Semantic Verification
          |
          v
Verified Alternative
          |
          v
Cost Comparison
          |
          v
Selected Transformation
          |
          v
PCIR Reverification
```

Conjectures remain separate from authoritative semantic facts until their obligations are discharged.

### 19.3 Typed E-graphs

E-graph equality classes are scoped by relevant types, arithmetic models, effects, ownership, aliasing, provenance and failure behavior.

An ideal mathematical identity does not automatically establish a valid machine-level rewrite.

For example, floating-point reassociation requires the applicable arithmetic permissions.

A valid integer rewrite must honor modular width.

### 19.4 Closure defunctionalization

The optimizer replaces eligible closure construction and indirect invocation with direct scalar execution when their observable behavior is equivalent.

```text
MakeClosure(environment)
CallClosure(closure, argument)
DisposeClosure(closure)
```

becomes, when verified:

```text
DirectCall(captured_values, argument)
```

Further inlining removes the call boundary.

### 19.5 Pipeline and Chain fusion

Compatible `map`, `filter`, `fold` and Chain stages are fused when evaluation order, failures, ownership, effects, traps and allocation observations permit.

Pure mathematical equivalence alone does not authorize effectful transformations.

### 19.6 Reference and allocation elimination

Retain/release, allocation/free and disposal operations are removed only when the removed operations are provably unobservable under the governing contract.

Atomic synchronization, destructor effects, allocation failure and resource limits are preserved.

