## 97. Polr — Path Of Least Resistance


### 27.1 Official definition

POLR is SAGE's verified, constraint-aware engineering navigation system.

It identifies the least costly valid route from an existing program state to a declared objective.

The selected route satisfies all mandatory semantic, security, resource, ownership and compatibility requirements.

POLR minimizes unnecessary engineering resistance while preserving correctness.

### 27.2 Governing law

**The path of least resistance is the least costly valid path under the complete set of governing obligations and the declared search scope.**

### 27.3 Seven principles

1. Correctness precedes convenience.
2. Safety precedes optimization.
3. Valid reuse precedes unnecessary reconstruction.
4. Changes remain as narrow as correctness permits.
5. Evidence precedes certainty.
6. Trade-offs remain explicit.
7. Identical declared inputs produce deterministic route selection.

### 27.4 Navigation pipeline

```text
PROGRAMMING OBJECTIVE
          |
          v
Understand Intended Outcome
          |
          v
Locate Relevant Blueprint Regions
          |
          v
Collect Verified Knowledge
          |
          v
Identify Constraints
          |
          v
Generate Candidate Routes
          |
          v
Eliminate Invalid Routes
          |
          v
Evaluate Engineering Costs
          |
          v
Rank Feasible Alternatives
          |
          v
Discharge Proof Obligations
          |
          v
SELECT VALID ROUTE
          |
          v
Generate Implementation Guidance
          |
          v
Apply Authorized Changes
          |
          v
Validate and Update Blueprint
```

POLR is integrated with the SAGE Knowledge Model, PITEL and ACO.

